data dispatch_attempt_oracle_pin_layout_note: String = "The oracle pin is TWO one-fact files beside the attempt's other evidence, not one record needing a grammar. That follows the directory's existing shape — attempt-key, spawn-failure.txt and provider-events.jsonl are each one fact in one file — and it is what lets the verification side read a value back without a JSON parser, which this seam does not have. Only these two facts cross the disk seam because they are the only two that cannot be re-derived at verification time: what the oracle's content WAS before the agent started, and which revision that content came from. The subject, the selection, and the declared command are all re-derived from the node's own execution contract, so persisting them would be a second home for a fact that already has one."

