data dispatch_event_pipe_seam_note: String = "tmux pipe-pane is the one foreign-executor seam in attempt capture: upstream requires a shell-command payload. TmuxPipeCommand bounds that residue. The earlier session-environment design was rejected by live execution because pipe processes did not inherit tmux set-environment values and created no file. Staging order is state directory -> idle exact-shell pane -> default-shell -> remain-on-exit -> quoted pipe -> typed provider respawn, so the first provider byte and a fast nonzero exit are both observable. The payload itself is no longer constructed here: gunbc.dispatch_pipe_pane_emit builds it as a bash AST and renders it through the signed serializer (review 44063), which is why this module now imports an EMISSION rather than joining a command: a serializer refusal has no command to hand back, so dispatch_spawn_commands_for_instance refuses the whole plan instead of staging one (review 44113)."

// THE PUBLICATION DIRECTORY IS PREPARED WITH THE ATTEMPT DIRECTORY, IN ONE install -d, and the
// reason it is here rather than on the write path is that the write path cannot create it. The
// Filesystem.Write intrinsic is a bare write with no parent creation, and it emits its
// `[file] write <path>` trace BEFORE attempting -- so a publication receipt written into a
// directory that does not exist logs exactly like a successful write and fails with ENOENT, which
// is how this went unnoticed. std.realization_schedule.Measured on srv1 2026-08-19: zero of twelve attempt directories had
// a publication/ subdirectory, and every publish pass reported failed while the journal showed the
// write line for each one.
//
// It is not a deploy member either, and that distinction is the whole design point. The receipts
// directory (gunbc.host_layout instance_receipts_dir) IS bootstrapped at apply time because there
// is exactly one per instance; a publication directory belongs to an ATTEMPT, which is minted at
// runtime long after any apply, so a deploy member could only ever create directories that do not
// exist yet. The attempt's own prepare step is the earliest moment the path is known.
//
// install -d takes a list, so this is the same single command with a second directory rather than
// a new step -- the attempt directory and the one subdirectory it is required to contain come into
// existence together, and publication_receipt_directory_is_named_once_note's requirement that a
// reader be able to LIST the directory holds from attempt birth instead of from first publish.
fn attempt_state_prepare_argv_for_instance(
  instance: gunbc.roadmap_dashboard_instance.HostDashboardInstance,
  node_id: gunbc.roadmap_model.RoadmapNodeId,
  attempt_key: String,
) -> HostExecArgv {
  host_exec_argv(
    program: dispatch_capability_program(
      environment: instance.execution_environment,
      cap: AttemptStateDirectoryCapability,
    ),
    args: [
      "-d",
      "-m", "0700",
      dispatch_attempt_state_path_for_instance(
        instance: instance,
        node_id: node_id,
        attempt_key: attempt_key,
      ),
      dispatch_attempt_publication_dir_for_instance(
        instance: instance,
        node_id: node_id,
        attempt_key: attempt_key,
      ),
    ],
  )
}

